  "description": "Host-side NVLink port enumeration, nvidia-imex service state and DCGM NVLink bandwidth for the GB300 estate. Every aggregate has an exactly-matching worklist beneath it. No IB, UFM or switch dependencies.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "<div style=\"font:13px/1.55 Inter,Roboto,sans-serif;color:#c7d0d9\"><div style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:600;color:#e6edf3;margin-bottom:4px\">GPU NVLink Health &mdash; link enumeration and bandwidth</div><div style=\"color:#8b98a5;margin-bottom:8px\">Host-side NVLink port state from the tray-resident collector (<code>su1_nvlink_up</code>, 131k port series across SU1&ndash;SU7 &mdash; the <code>su1_</code> prefix is a collector name, not a scope) and the DCGM NVLink bandwidth counter. A healthy GB300 GPU enumerates 18 NVLink ports. Tray-level lane totals (72 per tray) and the <code>nvidia-imex</code> service live on the <a href=\"/d/nvis-nvlink-downlanes/?${__url_time_range}\" style=\"color:#6ea8fe;text-decoration:none\">NVLink Downlane Map</a>, which owns those two datasets for the whole estate.</div><div style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#8b98a5\">GPU area&nbsp;&rsaquo;&nbsp;</span><a href=\"/d/nvis-l2-gpu-health/?${__url_time_range}\" style=\"color:#6ea8fe;text-decoration:none\">Area home</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"/d/gpu-health/?${__url_time_range}\" style=\"color:#6ea8fe;text-decoration:none\">Coverage &middot; thermal &middot; power &middot; clocks</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"/d/gpu-errors/?${__url_time_range}\" style=\"color:#6ea8fe;text-decoration:none\">Error surface &mdash; ECC &middot; XID &middot; violations</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color:#e6edf3;font-weight:600\">NVLink &amp; bandwidth</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"/d/nvis-dcgm-diag/?${__url_time_range}\" style=\"color:#6ea8fe;text-decoration:none\">Readiness checks</a></div></div>",
        "mode": "html"
      },
      "title": "",
      "transparent": true,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "id": 2,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "NVLink port enumeration \u2014 per GPU, host side",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Total NVLink ports reporting state UP. The per-rack table below decomposes it \u2014 its \"Ports UP\" column sums to this number. The collector publishes a port series only while the port is up, so a missing port shows up as a GPU with fewer than 18 links rather than as a DOWN port.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "noValue": "0",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "locale"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
